What will be the value of `fd` and the file size after executing the following code?
```c
int fd = open("file.txt", O_WRONLY | O_CREAT | O_TRUNC, 0644);
write(fd, "ABC", 3);
write(fd, "DEF", 3);
close(fd);
```

What is the output of the following code snippet?
```c
int fd = open("test.txt", O_RDWR | O_CREAT | O_TRUNC, 0644);
write(fd, "HELLO", 5);
lseek(fd, 0, SEEK_SET);
char buf[10];
read(fd, buf, 5);
buf[5] = '\0';
printf("%s", buf);
close(fd);
```

Consider this code. What is the most likely problem and its consequence?
```c
int fd = open("data.bin", O_RDONLY);
if (fd == -1) {
    perror("open");
}
char buffer[100];
read(fd, buffer, 100);
write(fd, "test", 4);
close(fd);
```

What is the result of this sequence, and why?
```c
int fd = open("data.txt", O_WRONLY | O_CREAT | O_APPEND, 0644);
lseek(fd, 10, SEEK_SET);
write(fd, "X", 1);
close(fd);
```

